SUMMARY:Neptune Diner Meetup June!
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nWe will be meeting for brunch a
 t a local diner! This one is a bit later in the morning than usual for tho
 se who like to sleep in!\n\nNeptune Diner\n924 N. Prince St.\nLancaster PA
  17603\n\nNeptune Diner is on the right side of the one-way Prince St. It 
 has its own sizable parking lot adjacent. If you pass the Baseball stadium
  you've gone too far!\n\nWe look forward to seeing you!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 314836929/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260517T223828Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T223828Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Lancaster Freethought Society
UID:event_315036804@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260603T045607Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260606T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260606T173000
SUMMARY:Old School Discussion: Consciousness-Raising Revisited
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n***Week 2 — Work\, Caregiving
 \, and Invisible Labor: What work keeps life functioning\, and who does it
 ?***\nBefore social media\, people gathered in small groups to discuss how
  society shapes personal life. During the Second Wave feminist movement\, 
 consciousness-raising groups became a powerful tool for understanding the 
 connection between personal experience and larger social systems.\nWomen a
 nd men are welcome.\n\nThis is not therapy\, debate club\, or partisan org
 anizing. It is a structured discussion format built around listening\, ref
 lection\, and lived experience.\nEach session includes:\n\n* 3-minute spea
 king rounds\n* equal participation\n* the option to pass\n* attentive list
 ening without interruption or debate\n* guided discussion around a weekly 
 theme (90 minutes)\n* informal conversation and socializing afterward (30 
 minutes)\n\nFacilitated by Susan Guggenheim\, LFS member.\nLimited to 10 p
 articipants.\nAttend one session or several. Regular attendance is encoura
 ged\, but not required.\nNo homework. No expertise required.\nJust curiosi
 ty\, honesty\, and active listening.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315036804/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260531T121330Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260531T121330Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Lancaster Freethought Society
UID:event_314836951@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260603T045607Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T120000
SUMMARY:LFS Walk in the Park!
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nJust a hike around the park\, e
 njoying the weather!\n\nThis event is pet-friendly! Consider bringing wate
 r and snacks. Wear appropriate shoes\, bring water shoes if you would like
  to wade in the river. Sunscreen recommended. Mix of paved trails and dirt
  trails\, some trails might require a moderate climb. The park offers rest
 room facilities. In the event of weather we'll instead meet at Pavilion 1 
 and chat!\n\nAfter crossing the Strawberry St. bridge over the Conestoga r
 iver to enter the park\, there is a parking lot downhill to the left (pict
 ured above). We will meet 9:00am - 9:15am\, pick a route\, and walk!\n\n(I
 f you have difficulty finding the spot on GPS\, try: 38 Pontz Dr\, Lancast
 er\, PA 17602)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 314836951/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260517T224323Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T224323Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Lancaster Freethought Society
UID:event_314836958@meetup.com
